---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "APR and Points: When a lower rate pays off";
const description =
  "Learn how points affect APR and when they pay off based on your time horizon. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Points break-even</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>APR and points break-even</h1>
    <p>
      Paying points can lower the rate, but the upfront cost needs time to pay off. This guide shows how to compare points
      using APR and a break-even horizon.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR comparison inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount and term (keep them constant across offers).</li>
      <li>Nominal rate vs APR and which fees are included.</li>
      <li>Upfront fees paid in cash vs financed.</li>
      <li>Expected time horizon before refinance or payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Break-even logic</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Points are paid upfront to reduce the rate.</li>
      <li>Monthly savings accumulate over time.</li>
      <li>Break-even = upfront cost / monthly savings.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Run the APR calculator with and without points.</li>
      <li>Calculate the monthly payment difference.</li>
      <li>Compare break-even to your expected horizon.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Inputs to collect first</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Total points cost in dollars.</li>
      <li>Rate difference with and without points.</li>
      <li>Planned years in the home or before refinance.</li>
      <li>Any lender credits that offset other fees.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Break-even checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Calculate the monthly payment savings from points.</li>
      <li>Divide point cost by monthly savings for break-even months.</li>
      <li>Compare break-even to your planned horizon.</li>
      <li>Re-run if the rate, fees, or term changes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Buying points when you might refinance soon.</li>
      <li>Ignoring lender credits that may be a better fit.</li>
      <li>Comparing points across different terms.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Cash available for points without draining reserves.</li>
      <li>Expected holding period for the loan.</li>
      <li>Rate difference in payment dollars per month.</li>
      <li>Alternative use for the upfront cash.</li>
      <li>Any rate float or lock timing constraints.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario notes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare break-even against a refinance timeline.</li>
      <li>Use conservative estimates for monthly savings.</li>
      <li>Include taxes if points are deductible in your case.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-comparison-checklist">APR and prepayment</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do points always lower APR?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Often yes, but the benefit depends on term and fee size. Compare both scenarios.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can points be financed?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Sometimes. Financing points can raise total cost; compare both approaches.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Compare points scenarios</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>




